        <div class="lg-body">
          <p class="lg-updated">Last updated: November 13, 2026</p>
          <div class="lg-intro">
<p>MAD Funnel Design is the independent web design and development practice of Aldrich Matthew Domingo, based in the Philippines. This website presents my work, explains the services I offer, and provides a way for prospective clients to discuss their projects.</p>
<p>By using this website, you agree to the terms below. They explain the boundaries of using my website and the general expectations surrounding my services.</p>
          </div>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-01" aria-labelledby="t-01-title">
          <h2 id="t-01-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">01</span>Using This Website</h2>
<p>You’re welcome to browse my work, read the information provided, share relevant pages, and contact me about a potential project.</p>
<p>What you cannot do is use this website in a way that interferes with its operation, compromises its security, or violates another person’s rights.</p>
<p>In particular, you must not:</p>
<ul><li>Attempt to access restricted areas, accounts, or systems without authorization.</li><li>Introduce malicious code, scripts, or other harmful material.</li><li>Use the website to distribute unlawful or deceptive content.</li><li>Copy website materials and present them as your own.</li><li>Interfere with the experience or access of other visitors.</li></ul>
<p>Access to this website may be restricted where misuse or security concerns arise.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-02" aria-labelledby="t-02-title">
          <h2 id="t-02-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">02</span>The Work You See Here</h2>
<p>The projects presented on this website represent selected examples of my design and development work.</p>
<p>Some are created for clients. Others are independent concepts or demonstrations developed to explore a particular industry, visual direction, or website functionality.</p>
<p>A portfolio example is intended to show how I approach a design or technical challenge. It should not be interpreted as evidence of a client’s financial performance, business growth, or commercial results unless those results are explicitly documented.</p>
<p>Project appearances, features, and live links may change over time. A published screenshot may not always reflect the latest version of a website.</p>
<p>If you want to reference or reuse something from a project, please ask first. A publicly accessible portfolio does not mean its underlying design, code, or creative assets are free to reproduce.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-03" aria-labelledby="t-03-title">
          <h2 id="t-03-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">03</span>Ownership of Creative Work</h2>
<p>The designs, writing, visual compositions, branding elements, and original code published on this website are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.</p>
<p>Unless a specific item is identified as belonging to someone else, the materials created for MAD Funnel Design remain my intellectual property.</p>
<p>You may share links to my work and refer to it for legitimate informational purposes. You may not reproduce, resell, distribute, or modify my original work for commercial use without permission.</p>
<p>Client ownership is handled separately. The rights to a website, design, code, or other deliverables created through a paid engagement depend on the ownership and licensing arrangements agreed upon for that project.</p>
<p>Third-party assets, software, fonts, and platform components remain subject to their respective licenses.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-04" aria-labelledby="t-04-title">
          <h2 id="t-04-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">04</span>When You Contact Me</h2>
<p>The contact form, email, and scheduling links are provided so you can ask questions or discuss a possible project.</p>
<p>Sending an inquiry does not mean that a project has been accepted, a price has been agreed upon, or a working relationship has started.</p>
<p>Before work begins, the project details should be confirmed in writing. This includes the agreed scope, deliverables, fees, payment arrangements, timeline, and any other relevant conditions.</p>
<p>I may decline an inquiry if the requested work does not align with my services, technical capabilities, availability, or working arrangements.</p>
<p>Please provide accurate information when submitting an inquiry. Do not include passwords, payment-card details, or other confidential information in an ordinary contact form.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-05" aria-labelledby="t-05-title">
          <h2 id="t-05-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">05</span>What a Project Includes</h2>
<p>Every website or development engagement is different. The actual work depends on what has been discussed and approved for that project.</p>
<p>A proposal or written agreement will define what is included and what falls outside the agreed scope.</p>
<p>A request for additional pages, features, integrations, revisions, or functionality after approval may require a separate quotation.</p>
<p>Project schedules also depend on both sides. Delayed content, missing access, late feedback, or pending approvals can affect delivery dates.</p>
<p>You are responsible for ensuring that materials supplied for your project, including text, photographs, logos, and other assets, are accurate and that you have permission to use them.</p>
<p>Project-specific agreements take priority over these general terms when they address the same subject in greater detail.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-06" aria-labelledby="t-06-title">
          <h2 id="t-06-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">06</span>What a Website Can and Cannot Guarantee</h2>
<p>A well-designed website can make information easier to understand, improve the way a business presents itself, and provide a clearer path for visitors to take action.</p>
<p>It cannot guarantee what visitors will do.</p>
<p>Search visibility, AI-generated recommendations, inquiries, bookings, sales, and revenue depend on many factors beyond website design and development.</p>
<p>These may include market demand, competition, pricing, business operations, content quality, search engine changes, advertising activity, and third-party technology.</p>
<p>My work is intended to provide a considered design and technical implementation, not a promise of a particular commercial outcome.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-07" aria-labelledby="t-07-title">
          <h2 id="t-07-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">07</span>Tools and Services Outside My Control</h2>
<p>Some projects rely on external platforms to function. These may include website builders, e-commerce systems, hosting providers, analytics services, scheduling software, CRM platforms, and automation tools.</p>
<p>Their availability, pricing, features, and policies can change independently of my work.</p>
<p>If a third-party service experiences downtime, changes its functionality, limits an account, or discontinues a feature, I cannot guarantee that the affected functionality will remain available.</p>
<p>Unless a separate maintenance or support arrangement is agreed upon, ongoing subscriptions, platform fees, hosting costs, and third-party service charges are the client’s responsibility.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-08" aria-labelledby="t-08-title">
          <h2 id="t-08-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">08</span>Information and Website Tracking</h2>
<p>When you visit this website or contact me, certain information may be processed to support communication, website functionality, security, and performance measurement.</p>
<p>For example, this may include information you submit directly, such as your name, email address, business details, and project requirements.</p>
<p>Depending on the tools enabled, technical information may also be collected through analytics, cookies, or similar technologies.</p>
<p>I use relevant information to respond to inquiries, discuss projects, maintain the website, understand visitor activity, and meet applicable legal obligations.</p>
<p>I do not sell personal information.</p>
<p>The specific information collected, the services involved, and the choices available to you are explained in the separate Privacy Policy.</p>
<p><strong>Read the Privacy Policy:</strong> <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-09" aria-labelledby="t-09-title">
          <h2 id="t-09-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">09</span>External Websites</h2>
<p>You may find links to other websites throughout this site, including live portfolio projects, scheduling services, software platforms, and other resources.</p>
<p>Once you leave MAD Funnel Design, the policies and practices of the destination website apply.</p>
<p>I do not control the operation, content, security, or availability of external websites and cannot take responsibility for changes made to them.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-10" aria-labelledby="t-10-title">
          <h2 id="t-10-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span>Responsibility and Limitations</h2>
<p>I take reasonable care in maintaining this website and presenting information about my work.</p>
<p>However, the website is provided for general information and may occasionally contain outdated information, broken links, interruptions, or technical errors.</p>
<p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, I am not responsible for losses arising solely from a visitor’s reliance on general website information or temporary inability to access this website.</p>
<p>This section does not remove rights or protections that cannot legally be excluded. Work performed under a separate client agreement is subject to the responsibilities and limitations established in that agreement and applicable law.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-11" aria-labelledby="t-11-title">
          <h2 id="t-11-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span>Changes to This Page</h2>
<p>As the services and website develop, these terms may need to change.</p>
<p>When that happens, the revised version will appear on this page with a new update date. The version published here applies to your subsequent use of the website, subject to applicable law.</p>
<p>For an existing client engagement, changes to these general website terms do not automatically replace the terms already agreed upon for that project.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-12" aria-labelledby="t-12-title">
          <h2 id="t-12-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span>Applicable Law</h2>
<p>These Terms are intended to be interpreted in accordance with the applicable laws of the Republic of the Philippines, subject to mandatory legal protections and any other applicable jurisdictional requirements.</p>
<p>Any dispute will be handled through the appropriate legal process and competent forum under applicable law.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lg-sec" id="t-13" aria-labelledby="t-13-title">
          <h2 id="t-13-title"><span class="lg-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span>Get in Touch</h2>
<p>If something on this page needs clarification, or you have a question about using this website, you can reach me through:</p>
<h3>MAD Funnel Design</h3>
<p>Website: <a href="https://www.madfunneldesign.com">https://www.madfunneldesign.com</a></p>
<p>Email: <a href="mailto:madfunneldesign@gmail.com">madfunneldesign@gmail.com</a></p>
<p>Location: Philippines</p>
        </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

